= State and Local Affairs

Governors, legislatures, and secretaries of state decide how elections are run and how policy is lived. Where do we fight?

- @legislatures: Flip state legislatures
- @secretaries: Back secretary of state candidates
- @ballot_measures: Pursue ballot initiatives
- @governors_races: Invest in governors races
- @easy_discard

@legislatures
subtitle: -1 resource
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: resources -= 1; dem_legislatures += 1; gerrymander_bias -= 0.15; civic_strength += 100; month_actions += 1

Targeted spending in legislative races begins to pay off.

@secretaries
subtitle: -1 resource
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: resources -= 1; election_admin += 3; subversion_progress -= 0.3; month_actions += 1

Election administration races become a priority.

@ballot_measures
subtitle: -1 resource
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: resources -= 1; gerrymander_bias -= 0.3; voting_rights += 0.1; dem_enthusiasm += 0.3; month_actions += 1

Voters approve independent redistricting commissions and voting access measures.

@governors_races
subtitle: -1 resource
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: resources -= 1; dem_governors += 1; rural_dem += 1*(1-dissent); month_actions += 1

A strong bench of governors produces future leaders.
